{"autose": "session-start", "role": "judge", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "label": "r0-requirements-1", "attempt": 0, "prompt": "Acceptance criteria:\n- AC-FR-001-1: Given the text `[a](https://example.com)`, when `markdown.markdown(text, extensions=['external_links'])` is called, then no exception is raised.\n- AC-FR-001-2: Given an instance `markdown.Markdown(extensions=['external_links'])`, when `convert('text')` is called, then the result is `<p>text</p>`.\n- AC-FR-002-1: Given the text `[a](https://example.com)`, when `markdown.markdown(text)` is called, then the result is `<p><a href=\"https://example.com\">a</a></p>`.\n- AC-FR-002-2: Given the text `<https://example.com>`, when `markdown.markdown(text)` is called with no extensions, then the result contains neither `target=` nor `rel=`.\n- AC-FR-003-1: Given the text `[a](https://example.com)` and the extension enabled, when converted, then the output contains one `<a` start tag whose attributes include `href=\"https://example.com\"`, `target=\"_blank\"` and `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`.\n- AC-FR-003-2: Given the text `[a](http://example.com/x?y=1)` and the extension enabled, when converted, then the `<a` start tag includes `target=\"_blank\"` and `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`.\n- AC-FR-003-3: Given the text `[a](https://example.com)` and the extension enabled, when converted, then the link text and `href` are unchanged: the output contains `href=\"https://example.com\"` and `>a</a>`.\n- AC-FR-004-1: Given the text `<https://example.com>` and the extension enabled, when converted, then the `<a` start tag includes `href=\"https://example.com\"`, `target=\"_blank\"` and `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`.\n- AC-FR-004-2: Given the text `<mailto:a@example.com>` or `<a@example.com>` and the extension enabled, when converted, then the output contains neither `target=` nor `rel=`.\n- AC-FR-005-1: Given the text `[a][1]` followed by a blank line and `[1]: https://example.com`, with the extension enabled, when converted, then the `<a` start tag includes `target=\"_blank\"` and `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`.\n- AC-FR-006-1: Given the text `[a](/docs/page.html)` and the extension enabled, when converted, then the result is `<p><a href=\"/docs/page.html\">a</a></p>`.\n- AC-FR-006-2: Given the text `[a](#section)` and the extension enabled, when converted, then the result is `<p><a href=\"#section\">a</a></p>`.\n- AC-FR-006-3: Given the text `[a](mailto:a@example.com)` and the extension enabled, when converted, then the output contains neither `target=` nor `rel=`.\n- AC-FR-006-4: Given the text `[a](page.html)` and the extension enabled, when converted, then the result is `<p><a href=\"page.html\">a</a></p>`.\n- AC-FR-007-1: Given the text `![alt](https://example.com/i.png)` and the extension enabled, when converted, then the result is `<p><img alt=\"alt\" src=\"https://example.com/i.png\" /></p>`.\n- AC-FR-007-2: Given the text `[![alt](https://example.com/i.png)](https://example.com)` and the extension enabled, when converted, then the `<a` start tag includes `target=\"_blank\"` and `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`, and the `<img` tag contains neither `target=` nor `rel=`.\n- AC-FR-008-1: Given the extension named `external_links`, when `markdown.markdown('[a](https://example.com)', extensions=['external_links'])` is called, then no configuration is needed and the output matches AC-FR-003-1."}
